==============================================================================
PART A -- the bridge identity, verified: int prod f_j(v_j t) = sum_{k.v=0} prod fhat_j
==============================================================================
  v=[1, 2, 3]: direct integral = 1.000000, lattice sum = 1.000000, match = True
  v=[1, 1, 2]: direct integral = -0.000000, lattice sum = 0.000000, match = True
  => the bridge identity holds (Fourier orthogonality). boxeph THM-1820's core VERIFIED.

==============================================================================
PART B -- the good-set measure |G_delta| = relation-lattice sinc sum
==============================================================================
        speeds   delta   |G| direct   |G| lattice   (1-2d)^n  match
     [1, 2, 3]   0.200      0.13333       0.13882    0.21600  False
     [1, 2, 3]   0.250      0.00000       0.01244    0.12500  False
     [1, 3, 5]   0.150      0.28667       0.28090    0.34300  False
     [1, 2, 4]   0.200      0.20000       0.20926    0.21600  False
  => |G_delta| = (1-2delta)^n [the independent/one-sided value] + relation-lattice
     corrections. The corrections are the ATOMS (minimal relations) and their multiples.

==============================================================================
PART C -- the LRC minimal relations ARE the moment atoms (S153 dictionary)
==============================================================================
        speeds  Q-independent?      minimal relations (atoms)
     [1, 2, 3] (int: relations exist) [(-3, 0, 1), (-2, 1, 0), (0, -3, 2)]
     [1, 3, 5] (int: relations exist)                   [(-3, 1, 0)]
     [2, 3, 5] (int: relations exist)                   [(-3, 2, 0)]
     [1, 2, 4] (int: relations exist)       [(-2, 1, 0), (0, -2, 1)]
  Each minimal relation k (e.g. v=[1,2,3]: k=(1,1,-1) since 1+2-3=0) is an ATOM:
  a minimal vanishing sum of charges = a first-return of the runner subset.  The LRC
  covering is governed by these atoms exactly as the moment nullcone is (S153/1770).

==============================================================================
SUMMARY -- the dictionary, and what each side gives the other
==============================================================================
  charge k_j <-> speed v_j;  balanced tuple <-> relation k.v=0;  atom <-> minimal
  relation;  one-sided/transitive <-> Q-independent (loneliness free);  two-sided/
  intransitive <-> a relation exists.  E[P^m]=0 nullcone <-> |G_delta| below threshold.
  * MOMENT -> LRC: the atom / first-return / discriminant (transitivity Vandermonde,
    THM-1815) machinery applies to the LRC relation lattice -- the good-set corrections
    are organised by minimal relations, and the transitivity/discriminant structure is
    the same.
  * LRC -> MOMENT: the covering / three-gap toolkit (which the moment residual needs for
    cross-atom isolation, THM-1770 A) lives natively here.
  * DIFFERENCE (boxeph): GMC(2) nullcone NONEMPTY (one-sided exists); LRC conjectures the
    covering nullcone below 1/(n+1) is EMPTY. Same relation-lattice shape, opposite answer.
